ry declares, never the shipped tree, so a kit file the inventory omits altogether is outside all of them; and the installer is excluded from its own inventory in prose at its module rather than as a row in the exclusion carrier, so the one exclusion that is load-bearing for the distribution model is the one no reader can enumerate mechanically.\"\"\"\n rationale = \"\"\"Naming the inventory that exists rather than a purpose-coverage checker that does not is what keeps this row falsifiable: the universe, the exclusion carrier and two of the four finding classes are delivered and already driven by tests, so what the parent is owed is a JOIN and a widened universe, not a new mechanism. Recording the three gaps ON the row is the load-bearing half - a design row naming only the delivered arms would read as though the obligation were discharged, and the next reviser would have to re-derive by inspection that the inventory carries no requirement reference anywhere in it. The alternative, minting a row for a coverage checker with an invented module and symbol, is refused on the evidence discipline the parent's tier already applies: a cited symbol must exist to be read.\"\"\"\n test_refs = \"(see TC-199)\"\n-status = \"Drafted\"\n+status = \"Approved\"\n component = \"CMP-009\"\n phase = 5\n \n@@ -2151,7 +2151,7 @@ code_symbol = \"backlink_ids/scan_backlinks/read_backlink_min\"\n detail = \"\"\"backlink_ids is the ONE definition of a purpose declaration in the source surface: an Implements token OPENING a line, followed by spine ids, with a line whose token is preceded by prose declaring nothing at all - the tightening that stopped two sentences denying a link from being harvested as the link. scan_backlinks runs that grammar over the declared source roots and implements_report joins its result against the live design rows; read_backlink_min reads the threshold from the one policy home, and the report WARNS at exit zero below that threshold, failing only when the caller asks